---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { sourceLinks } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engine"
  description="Inside The Stars Don’t Wait’s from-scratch C++20 engine: architecture, space-scale precision, rendering, simulation, and tools."
  background="engine"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Engine / Implemented systems"
    title="The machinery behind the horizon."
    intro="Sol Engine is a from-scratch C++20 engine built specifically for a large, persistent space simulation. Its flight, rendering, simulation, UI, audio, data, and authoring systems have advanced through runnable milestones; the architecture below distinguishes that working foundation from release work still ahead."
  >
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button-secondary" href={sourceLinks.repository}
        >Browse source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
      <a class="button-secondary" href={sourceLinks.enginePlan}
        >Full engine plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="wide-container engine-stats" aria-label="Engine facts">
    <div><strong>C++20</strong><span>Exceptions off</span></div>
    <div><strong>Vulkan</strong><span>Custom rendering layer</span></div>
    <div><strong>60 Hz</strong><span>Fixed simulation tick</span></div>
    <div>
      <strong>12 suites</strong><span>Recorded in the current plan</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wide-container section-pad architecture-section">
    <div>
      <SectionHeading
        eyebrow="Architecture"
        title="Hard boundaries. Deliberate layers."
        intro="Each major module is a static library with dependencies enforced by the build graph. The game sits on the engine; lower layers cannot quietly reach upward."
      />
      <ol class="layer-list">
        <li>
          <span>08</span><strong>Game</strong><small>Content + game glue</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>07</span><strong>UI</strong><small
            >Custom game UI + dev overlay</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>06</span><strong>Scripting</strong><small
            >Lua 5.4 + explicit bindings</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>05</span><strong>Simulation</strong><small
            >Galaxy, economy, factions, missions</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>04</span><strong>ECS + assets</strong><small
            >State, data, hot reload</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>03</span><strong>Renderer</strong><small
            >HDR, impostors, particles</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>02</span><strong>RHI</strong><small
            >Vulkan resources + synchronization</small
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>01</span><strong>Core + platform</strong><small
            >Memory, jobs, Win32, input</small
          >
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <aside class="architecture-note panel">
      <p class="technical-label">Precision model</p>
      <div class="coordinate-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="axis axis-x"></span>
        <span class="axis axis-y"></span>
        <span class="origin"></span>
        <span class="point point-a"></span>
        <span class="point point-b"></span>
      </div>
      <h3>Double in simulation. Float at the camera.</h3>
      <p>
        World positions use double precision. Rendering subtracts a per-frame
        camera origin before converting to float, preserving stable visuals at
        solar-system distances.
      </p>
      <div class="architecture-proof">
        <strong>Demonstrated</strong>
        <span>127,000+ km scripted cruise at 10¹¹ m coordinates</span>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-pad">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Selected systems / Implemented"
      title="Tools for a simulation that has to keep moving."
    />
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">ECS / SPARSE SET</span>
        <h3>Data shaped by evidence</h3>
        <p>
          A representative benchmark selected sparse-set storage for thousands
          of ships and projectiles. Generational handles, queries, deferred
          commands, and versioned serialization form the state backbone.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">SIM / TWO FIDELITIES</span>
        <h3>Near detail, distant consequence</h3>
        <p>
          The current system runs at full fidelity. The wider galaxy advances
          through coarse agents, allowing traders, miners, markets, factions,
          and mission conditions to change beyond the player’s immediate view.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">DATA + TOOLS / FORGE</span>
        <h3>Author assets, then fly them</h3>
        <p>
          The Forge edits parametric and direct mesh geometry, builds LODs and
          procedural textures, writes validated model and content rows, and can
          receive Blender drops. Authored models reach the game through data
          rather than compiled model-name switches.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">UI / IN-REPO STACK</span>
        <h3>Player-facing, without a web layer</h3>
        <p>
          A custom immediate-mode renderer, cooked TrueType atlases, menu shell,
          HUD, station screens, maps, radar, and settings keep the game UI
          inside the engine. Dear ImGui remains a development tool.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">SIM / PERSISTENT SYSTEMS</span>
        <h3>Different loops, one saved world</h3>
        <p>
          Markets, production chains, faction relations, contracts, survey
          knowledge, depleted rocks, wrecks, fleets, and fittings all
          participate in explicit versioned state.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card panel">
        <span class="index">INPUT / PLAYTEST-DRIVEN</span>
        <h3>The screen says what the sim knows</h3>
        <p>
          Radar, map zoom, bookmarks, mission markers, direct selection, threat
          targeting, ship information, and rebindable controls were added from
          concrete playtest findings.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wide-container section-pad principles-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Engineering principles</p>
      <h2>Small enough to understand. Strong enough to extend.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="fact-list principles-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Purpose-built scope</strong>
        The engine and its Forge solve this game’s needs without general-purpose abstraction
        or speculative subsystems that no milestone requires.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deterministic systems</strong>
        Fixed-step simulation, seeded PRNG streams, and explicit save formats keep
        outcomes testable and state reproducible.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Debuggability from day one</strong>
        Validation, logs, debug draw, metrics, and the Dear ImGui development overlay
        expose systems while they are still being built.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Measured milestones</strong>
        Every phase ends in a runnable proof with exit criteria, tests, and documented
        caveats—not just an inventory of source files.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .engine-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .engine-stats > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .engine-stats > div:first-child {
    border-left: 0;
  }

  .engine-stats strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .engine-stats span {
    color: var(--color-dim);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  .architecture-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .layer-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .layer-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 8rem 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-top: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-surface-soft), transparent);
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .layer-list span {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  .layer-list strong {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .layer-list small {
    color: var(--color-dim);
  }

  .architecture-note {
    position: sticky;
    top: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }

  .coordinate-visual {
    position: relative;
    height: 15rem;
    margin-block: var(--space-6);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--color-line) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-line) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 2rem 2rem;
  }

  .axis {
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--color-line-strong);
  }

  .axis-x {
    top: 50%;
    right: 0;
    left: 0;
    height: 1px;
  }

  .axis-y {
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    width: 1px;
  }

  .origin,
  .point {
    position: absolute;
    width: 0.6rem;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .origin {
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    background: var(--color-text);
    box-shadow: 0 0 1rem var(--color-text);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }

  .point-a {
    top: 24%;
    left: 19%;
    background: var(--color-warm);
  }

  .point-b {
    right: 10%;
    bottom: 19%;
    background: var(--color-accent-bright);
  }

  .architecture-note > p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .architecture-proof {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .architecture-proof strong {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .architecture-proof span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .principles-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .principles-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (max-width: 58rem) {
    .architecture-section,
    .principles-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .architecture-note {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    .engine-stats,
    .principles-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .engine-stats > div:nth-child(3) {
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .engine-stats > div:nth-child(n + 3) {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }

    .layer-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    }

    .layer-list small {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
